0211: blueline bus votes down while the panel sleeps (bluebw_park=1, off by default)

An experiment for the ~210 mA screen-off draw: once the panel is in sleep,
the apps RSC's votes for the BCMs in bluebw_bcms (MC0 SH0 MM0-3) go to
Linux's keepalive (x 1, y 1); before it wakes, MM goes to its top and the
GPU's last DDR vote is put back. See bsd/dev/blueline_bw.c.

bluecensus=S (diagnostic): S seconds after the panel first sleeps, logs every
answering SPMI peripheral of SIDs 1, 3 and 5 (type, status, voltage, mode,
enable) and the main GDSC registers (gcc, dispcc mdss, gpucc cx/gx).
bw1: no change in draw (208 mA). See docs/LOG.md.

